  "notes": "OpenPilot on the 50 routes, 29 Oct 2026, one RTX PRO 6000 (shared), CARLA 0.9.15, six lanes. Driven at 20 Hz, which is openpilot's own rate and the benchmark protocol. One setup on every route: the tinygrad backend (PADDOCK_OPENPILOT_BACKEND=tinygrad), openpilot's own longitudinal plan (PADDOCK_OPENPILOT_NATIVE_LONG=1) and no driver-resume assistance (PADDOCK_OPENPILOT_RESUME_S=0). Driven from 9671b49 plus the TINYGRAD_ACTION_T fallback this commit adds to policy.py: the tinygrad ModelState has no long_action_t, so the native longitudinal planner raised AttributeError without it; the value is the 0.5 s the tinygrad path already feeds the model. Seven attempts failed on infrastructure and were re-run; their directories were moved out of this root, to _failed_infra beside it: node or CARLA start-up on 24795 (20261029T080029-0ffa0a), 3800 (20261029T080140-f99ef2), 2509 (20261029T080951-e076b4) and 26990 (20261029T095341-ac924f); the 2 h wall cap on the first attempts of 2084 (20261029T103048-d4e0c1), 2086 (20261029T104135-c8ba52) and 2050 (20261029T104914-1d3202), which ran at 3-4 s per tick under full CPU. It replaces the 30.09 typed in from docs/benchmarks/bench2drive.md (24 routes, unassisted estimate) as OpenPilot's Bench2Drive cell. 50 of 50 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to openpilot on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 50/50 source runs recorded.",
  "ingested_from": "op_b2d50_nativelong/bench2drive/openpilot"
